"""Refract Tips — what this OS does that Ubuntu doesn't, in one window.

WHY THIS EXISTS. Refract's distinguishing features are all invisible on a fresh
desktop. Modes, layouts, the top-bar switcher, the update path, Refract Monitor
and the distro-* commands are either behind a menu somebody has to notice or
behind a name they'd have to already know. gnome-initial-setup is purged and
masked (see hooks/0200-refract-identity.chroot), so there is no first-run wizard
either — a new owner gets a desktop and no indication that any of it is there.

WHAT IT DELIBERATELY IS NOT. A general Linux tutorial. Everything here is about
THIS system: nothing about apt, nothing about the terminal for its own sake,
nothing a GNOME user already knows. If a tip would be equally true on stock
Ubuntu, it does not belong.

Every row that names an action can PERFORM it. A tip about Refract Monitor with
no way to open Refract Monitor is a paragraph about a thing, not help.
"""
